    "q-79346": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79346",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\,\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and the $4$th columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1+1+2=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
